### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 15 - PHASE 64 REGRESSION SUITE
###
### This file tests every specific fix introduced in Phase 64.
### Run in order: Tier A → Tier B → Tier C → Tier D
###
### Phase 64 fixes map:
###
###   TIER A - Correctness (all production bugs):
###     A1: GovernanceLayer - hard limit fires before soft warning
###     A2: AgentDispatchHandler - AutonomyLevel no longer hardcoded SUPERVISED
###     A3: CompactionSummaryRepository - non-ASCII FTS5 search returns results
###     A4: TelegramMarkdownV2Renderer - headings render as bold not \#\# escape
###     A5: ReasoningStepParser - JSON parse error returns OBSERVE not FINISH
###     A6: CompactionHandler - fireAsync failure releases inFlight lock
###     A7: ChannelType.fromString - returns Optional.empty() not silent TELEGRAM
###
###   TIER B - Security:
###     B1: AuditEventRepository - TOCTOU race fixed via SessionAuditSequencer
###     B2: DevSecretSeeder - removed from ChatCommand, @IfBuildProfile("dev") only
###     B3: SessionResolutionHandler - UUID v3 (MD5) replaced with SessionRegistry
###
###   TIER C - Architecture:
###     C1: Session key is (channelType, channelId, userId) triplet
###     C2: ChannelCronNotificationDispatcher replaces Telegram-only observers
###     C3: GlobalKnowledgeBase uses rag_chunk table, not "rag:" prefix hack
###
###   TIER D - Quality:
###     D1: ContextCompactionService - Unicode-safe codepoint truncation
###     D2: GlobalKnowledgeBase - Locale.ROOT float serialization
###     D3: SqliteRetryTemplate - consolidated BUSY retry
###     D4: LlmModelFactory - deduplicated provider switch
###     D5: TelegramMarkdownV2Renderer.esc() - single-pass rewrite
###     D6: LangChainReasoningEngine - BudgetWarning not swallowed in structured output
###     D7: Dead code removed (SANDBOX_EXEC, RATE_LIMIT, System.out.println)
###
### Prerequisites: Amsha Agent serve mode, all Phase 64 fixes deployed,
###   AMSHA_LLM_API_KEY + GITHUB_TOKEN set
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# @baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080
# @validKey = key-internal-changeme


### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### TIER A - CORRECTNESS REGRESSION
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A1: Budget hard limit fires ON the call that exceeds it
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [A1-SETUP] Create session for budget ordering test
# @name a1Session
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [A1-TEST] Run tasks until budget is near limit, then push it over
# After this call, check audit for LOOP_BUDGET_EXCEEDED.
# If the fix was NOT applied, only BUDGET_EXCEEDED (warning) would appear
# and the next call would then fail - a one-call over-budget window.
# After the fix, LOOP_BUDGET_EXCEEDED appears on the call that crossed the limit.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{a1Session.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Write an exhaustive 800-word essay on Quarkus reactive programming model, covering Mutiny, RESTEasy Reactive, SmallRye Fault Tolerance, and integration with Hibernate Reactive.",
    "agentRole": "researcher",
    "maxIterations": 4
}

###

### [A1-VERIFY] Confirm LOOP_BUDGET_EXCEEDED in audit on this session
# Expect: eventType=LOOP_BUDGET_EXCEEDED present in audit events
# If NOT present yet (budget not reached), run A1-TEST again.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/session/{{a1Session.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{a1Session.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A2: FULL autonomy is NOT downgraded to SUPERVISED
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [A2-SETUP] Create session with FULL autonomy
# @name a2Session
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "autonomyLevel": "FULL"
}

###

### [A2-TEST] Run GitHub tool task - must complete WITHOUT approval pause
# If autonomy was silently downgraded to SUPERVISED, this returns 202 AWAITING_APPROVAL.
# After Phase 64-A fix A2: SessionResolutionHandler reads stored autonomy level from
# checkpoint and pushes it to MessageContext. AgentDispatchHandler uses that value
# instead of the hardcoded SUPERVISED constant.
# Expect: 200 Finished (answer contains GitHub data)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{a2Session.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "List the public repositories of GitHub user rsrini7.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [A2-VERIFY] Status must be COMPLETED, never AWAITING_APPROVAL
# If this returns AWAITING_APPROVAL - the fix was not applied.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{a2Session.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [A2-AUDIT] Confirm TOOL_INVOKED without APPROVAL_GRANTED in audit
# FULL autonomy: tool runs directly, no approval event needed.
# Expect: TOOL_INVOKED present, APPROVAL_GRANTED absent.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/session/{{a2Session.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{a2Session.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###


