# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# B3: Session IDs are random UUIDs from SessionRegistry (not MD5)
# Before: UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes(chatId+":"+userId) - MD5/UUID v3
# After: SessionRegistry.resolveOrCreate(channelType, channelId, userId)
#   → generates UUID.randomUUID() on first call, stores in session_registry,
#   → returns same UUID on subsequent calls for the same triplet.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [B3-SETUP] Create a session - UUID must be random (not MD5-derived)
# @name b3Session
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [B3-TEST] Run a simple task to verify session works with new UUID format
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{b3Session.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Confirm the session UUID is a random UUID (version 4), not an MD5-based UUID (version 3).",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{b3Session.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

